    <h1>Privacy Policy and Data Processing</h1>

    <h2>1. Our philosophy: privacy by design</h2>
    <p>Cuento is built on a Zero-PII (no personally identifiable information) model. We believe you should be able to create stories without leaving a digital footprint.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No email addresses:</strong> we do not collect or store email addresses.</li>
      <li><strong>No real-world data:</strong> your account is identified solely by the username you choose.</li>
      <li><strong>No tracking:</strong> we do not use tracking cookies and do not sell user data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Public content and narrative integrity</h2>
    <p>Cuento is a collaborative fiction environment. To preserve the logic and readability of the game world for all participants, game content — roleplay posts, character sheets, and wanted character listings — is considered part of the shared story. By registering on any Cuento instance, you grant the platform a perpetual licence to store and display this content to maintain narrative continuity, even after you leave. When an account is archived, this content is anonymised: the username is replaced with a standard identifier (for example, <code>The_Nameless_One</code>).</p>
    <p><strong>Severing the link:</strong> when an account is archived we permanently destroy the technical link between your credentials and your content. Once severed, this action is irreversible — we cannot associate posts with a new account because the link no longer exists in the database.</p>
    <div class="callout">All non-game data — posts in general (out-of-character) threads, account settings, and other personal content — is <strong>not</strong> anonymised or retained. It is permanently deleted when you use the data deletion tool described in section 3.</div>

    <h2>3. Direct messages and full data deletion</h2>
    <p>Your private correspondence and personal data belong to you alone. We provide a unique mechanism for permanently deleting them — even after you have left the platform.</p>
    <p><strong>Recovery codes:</strong> when you register, the system generates a set of unique recovery codes. Keep them in a safe place — they are the only cryptographic proof of ownership of your personal data.</p>
    <p><strong>Retained by default:</strong> when an account is archived or banned, direct messages remain accessible to your conversation partners by default to preserve conversation history. The link to your credentials is severed, but the messages themselves are stored until you choose to delete them.</p>
    <p><strong>Data deletion tool:</strong> using your recovery code, you can initiate permanent deletion of all non-game data associated with your account — at any time, without needing to log in and without requiring approval from admins or other participants. The following is deleted:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>All direct messages (DMs)</li>
      <li>Posts in general (out-of-character) threads</li>
      <li>Account settings and user preferences</li>
      <li>Any other non-game personal data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The following game content is <strong>not</strong> deleted — it is anonymised instead, to preserve narrative continuity for other players:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>In-game roleplay posts</li>
      <li>Character sheets</li>
      <li>Wanted character listings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. User responsibility and verification</h2>
    <p>Because we do not collect email addresses or other real-world identifiers, we have no way to verify your identity through traditional support channels.</p>
    <div class="callout">If you lose both your password and your recovery codes, we cannot recover your direct messages or delete your data on your behalf. Administrators can reset your password, but without the original encryption keys this will permanently destroy access to all previous direct messages.</div>

    <h2>5. Technical security</h2>
    <p>Direct messages are protected by cryptographically secure private keys. Your password, recovery codes, private keys, and message contents are never stored in plaintext.</p>
    <p>Neither site administrators nor developers can recover this information. This ensures that your correspondence remains confidential and accessible only to you and the people you message.</p>

    <h2>6. Regulatory compliance (GDPR and others)</h2>
    <p>By severing the link between credentials and content (anonymisation), Cuento satisfies the core principles of personal data protection legislation, including GDPR and CPPA.</p>
    <p>The data deletion tool directly implements the right to be forgotten, allowing permanent deletion of all non-game personal data even after the relationship with the platform has ended.</p>

